   "doc": "double-ended queue (ring buffer).\n\n`Deque<T>` is a ring buffer backed by a single heap allocation.\nBoth ends are O(1); growing doubles capacity and re-bases the\nbuffer at index 0 so the head/tail pointers don't have to wrap on\nthe new buffer. Capacity is always a power of two so modulo is a\nbit-and.\n\nLayout invariants:\n  * `head` is the index of the front element (when len > 0).\n  * Elements at indices `head, (head+1) & mask, ..., (head+len-1) & mask`\n    are live.\n  * `head` and `len` are stored as `usize`. `mask = cap - 1`.",
