   "doc": "the compiler-recognized intrinsic surface.\n\nThese declarations name operations the codegen lowers directly to LLVM\nIR or to libc calls, rather than to a yoop function body. They are in\nscope only when you import this file. As with anything under std/, value\nimports from here must use the namespace form:\n\n    import * as intr from \"std/core/intrinsics.yoop\";\n    let buf: int32[] = intr.heapAlloc(8);\n    intr.heapFree(buf);",
   "exports": []
