   "doc": "numeric parsing and small integer helpers.\n\nThe parsing direction only, and only from BYTES: `parseBytesToInt32` reads a\nsigned integer in any radix from 2 to 36 and returns a `Result` rather than\na sentinel, so a bad digit is a value you have to handle. The rendering\ndirection lives in std/core/format.yoop (`intToString` / `uintToString`).\n\n`nextPow2Floor8` is the growth-policy helper the containers share.\n\n    import * as num from \"std/core/numbers.yoop\";\n    switch (num.parseBytesToInt32(intr.stringAsBytes(\"ff\"), 16)) { ... }",
