     "signature": "export trait WithContext<T>",
     "doc": "Context-attaching `?`. `expr? \"loading config\"` prepends a\nmessage to the propagated error. When both Err payloads are plain strings\nthe compiler concatenates `\"<context>: <err>\"` itself and no impl is\nneeded; for any other payload type the operand's Err type must implement\n`WithContext<TargetErr>`, and the failure branch calls\n`WithContext.withContext(ref operandErr, context)` to build the outer Err\npayload.\n\nLike `Into<T>`, the source type is `self` and the target is the type\nparameter, so a same-shape impl reads `ParsingError implements\nWithContext<ParsingError>`. The impl decides where the context lands - a\nmessage prefix, a separate field, or an accumulated breadcrumb list - and\nit doubles as the cross-shape conversion, so one impl covers both.",
