     "signature": "export async sendOn( ref c: Client, ref req: ClientRequest, ref u: Uri, ref r: Reader, ref w: Writer, ): Result<ClientResponse, HttpError> propagates<disposable>",
     "doc": "Run one HTTP exchange over a connection the CALLER owns.\n\nThis is the whole client minus the socket. `send` above is this plus\n`tcpConnect`; `std/https` is this plus `tlsConnect`. Anything that can\npresent a `Reader` and a `Writer` works - a TLS session, a unix socket, a\ntunnel through a proxy, or a pair of in-memory buffers in a test.\n\nThe caller owns the connection and must keep it alive for the whole call:\nthe vtables hold pointers, and deliberately do not carry `Disposable`.\n\n`u` is passed rather than re-parsed so a caller that already resolved the\nURL (to decide how to connect, say) does not do it twice, and so a tunnel\ncan rewrite the target it asks for.",
