     "doc": "`serve` with the default limits.\n\nNote there is no `serveN<H implements Handler>` convenience wrapper that\nerases the handler for you: `Dispatcher.from(ref h)` needs a concrete\nstruct receiver and rejects a type parameter, so the erasure has to happen\nat a call site that knows the handler's real type. One line at the top of\nmain, and in exchange the serve loop exists exactly once in the binary:\n\n    let d: Dispatcher = Dispatcher.from(ref handler);\n    let served: int32 = http.serveDefault(ref lr.listener, ref d, 0)?;",
