     "doc": "A broken-down calendar time.\n\nWritten the way a human writes them, not the way `struct tm` stores them:\n`month` is 1-12 and `year` is the full year. `weekday` is 0 = Sunday and\n`yearday` is 0-based, both matching C.\n\n`utcOffsetMinutes` is this time's offset from UTC - 0 for a UTC value, and\nwhatever the zone and daylight-saving rules say for a local one. It is a\nfield rather than a global because the offset is a property of the INSTANT,\nnot of the machine: the same computer is at -300 in January and -240 in\nJuly.",
     "shape": "export type DateTime implements Display {\n    year: int32,\n    month: int32,\n    day: int32,\n    hour: int32,\n    minute: int32,\n    second: int32,\n    weekday: int32,\n    yearday: int32,\n    utcOffsetMinutes: int32,\n    // False when the conversion failed - an epoch the platform's time_t\n    // cannot represent. Every other field is then zero.\n    ok: bool,\n\n    // ISO-8601, which is the only rendering that sorts correctly as text and\n    // is unambiguous across locales.\n    function toString(ref self): string {\n        return iso8601(self);\n    }\n}",
